# Backend API base URL for the frontend (Create React App).
#
# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT: leave empty. Relative /api/v1 requests are proxied to
# http://localhost:8000 by the CRA "proxy" field in package.json — no CORS.
#
# PRODUCTION (Vercel): leave UNSET or EMPTY. The production build now ignores
# this value and always uses same-origin /api/v1 requests. The /api and /uploads
# rewrites in frontend/vercel.json forward them to the Suga backend, so the
# browser only resolves the VijayCart domain. This is required because the JWT
# cookie belongs to the Vercel origin, not the raw backend hostname.
#
# A stale value such as https://3pkgfqwokqax-production-rcqexbsf.us-central1.suga.run
# used to be baked into the CRA bundle and caused /api/v1/myprofile to return
# 401 after Google login. Remove it from Vercel even though the code now ignores it.
REACT_APP_API_URL=
